  "facts": [
    "The Lærdal Tunnel, opened on 27 November 2000, stretches 24.51 kilometres, making it the world’s longest road tunnel and the final link that allowed nonstop car travel between Oslo and Bergen without ferries.",
    "During its five‑year construction, workers blasted 2.5 million cubic metres of rock, creating three 6‑kilometre‑interval caves that feature blue lighting and yellow fringes to mimic sunrise and break driver monotony.",
    "Equipped with the first global air‑treatment plant, the tunnel pulls air through a 100‑metre cavern, filters out dust and nitrogen dioxide, and vents fresh air via fans at both entrances to keep drivers safe."
